Task 1: Create an Azure Resource Manager template
1. Azure portal -> Disk -> Storage Center | Azure Disks -> Create using : 
     Setting | Value |
    | --- | --- |
    | Subscription | *your subscription* | 
    | Resource Group | `az104-rg3` (If necessary, select **Create new**.)
    | Disk name | `az104-disk1` | 
    | Region | **East US** |
    | Availability zone | **No infrastructure redundancy required** | 
    | Source type | **None** |
    | Performance | **Standard HDD** (change size) |
    | Size | **32 Gib** | 
2. Go to resource -> Automation -> Export template
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Task 2: Edit an Azure Resource Manager template and then redeploy the template
1.Azure portal-> Search Deploy a custom template-> Custom deployment-> Quickstart template.
2. Build your own template in the editor -> Edit template-> Load file->  upload template.json that was downloaded.
3. Makes changes 
    + Change **disks_az104_disk1_name** to `disk_name` (two places to change)
    + Change **az104-disk1** to `az104-disk2` (one place to change)
4. Save
5. deployment settings:

    | Setting | Value |
    | --- |--- |
    | Subscription | *your subscription* |
    | Resource Group | `az104-rg3` |
    | Region | **(US) East US** |
    | Disk_name | `az104-disk2` |
6.Go to resource-> Verify az104-disk2 was created 
7.Verify Resource group az104-rg3 have two disks.
8.. Verify the template is in each disk 
